        "original_id": "2b3ecb1b-77ef-5555-9bd8-c86f917abb3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve, Onkaparinga River, Gulf St Vincent, Adelaide, Southern Adelaide\n- Concepts: marine protected areas, Kaurna language\n\nFacts:\n- Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve is a marine protected area in South Australia located in Gulf St Vincent adjoining the Adelaide metropolitan area.\n- Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve includes part of the Onkaparinga River and lies about 28 km south-west of Adelaide.\n- The Onkaparinga River is a river in the Southern Adelaide region of South Australia.\n- The Onkaparinga River is known as Ngangkiparri in the Kaurna language.",
